slftp Web UI Quickstart
Note: Web UI is early beta.

Prerequisites
- Node.js and npm installed (for building static assets).
- A running slftp instance with API enabled (see API_HOWTO).

Build Web UI
cd web-ui
npm install
npm run build

Built assets land in web-ui/dist/.

Windows (PowerShell) example:
cd .\web-ui
npm install
npm run build

Simplified Build Commands (Linux/Make)

For Linux users with Make installed, these commands automate the build and deployment process:

Frontend + Backend changes:
make all-with-ui WEB_DEPLOY_DIR=/your/slftp/path/web

This command:
1. Compiles the slftp backend (Pascal)
2. Copies the binary to the installation path
3. Builds the Web UI (npm run build)
4. Deploys the Web UI to the specified directory

Frontend-only changes:
make web-ui-deploy WEB_DEPLOY_DIR=/your/slftp/path/web

This command:
1. Builds the Web UI (npm run build)
2. Deploys the Web UI to the specified directory

These commands simplify the entire build and deployment workflow on Linux systems.

Deploy Web UI

At runtime, only the web/ folder in your slftp installation directory is needed; Node/npm is not required.

Linux/Mac:
# Deploy Web UI assets (clean old files first to avoid browser cache issues!)
# Assuming /your/slftp/path/ is your production directory
rm -rf /your/slftp/path/web/*
cp -r web-ui/dist/* /your/slftp/path/web/

Windows (PowerShell):
# Deploy Web UI assets (clean old files first!)
# Assuming C:\your\slftp\path\ is your production directory
Remove-Item -Recurse -Force C:\your\slftp\path\web\*
Copy-Item -Recurse -Force web-ui\dist\* C:\your\slftp\path\web\

Accessing the Web UI
URL: http://<host>:<port>/ (served from web/ folder by slftp)
You will be presented with a login screen. Enter the 'apikey' defined in your slftp.ini [api] section.

Web UI configuration
- The Web UI uses relative path '/api' to reach the API (same host/port)
- Host/port from slftp.ini [api] section apply to both Web UI and API automatically
- IRC Matches view uses ApiPrecatcherService/GetHits and ApiSystemService/GetRecentReleases
- For dev server: npm run dev (runs on http://localhost:5173)
  Set VITE_API_BASE_URL env var if connecting to remote API

Updating after code changes

If you changed frontend code (TypeScript/React files):
Linux/Mac:
1. Rebuild: cd web-ui && npm run build
2. Deploy: rm -rf /your/slftp/path/web/* && cp -r dist/* /your/slftp/path/web/
3. Hard-refresh browser: Ctrl+Shift+R (no slftp restart needed)

Windows:
1. Rebuild: cd web-ui; npm run build
2. Deploy: Remove-Item -Recurse -Force C:\your\slftp\path\web\*; Copy-Item -Recurse -Force dist\* C:\your\slftp\path\web\
3. Hard-refresh browser: Ctrl+Shift+R

If you changed API key in config:
1. Restart slftp to load new config
2. Login again in Web UI with new apikey (old token will be invalid)

Security notes
- Web UI now has authentication via login screen using the apikey from slftp.ini [api] section.
- The API token is stored in the browser's Local Storage after login.
- For production use, consider running behind nginx/traefik with TLS to protect the apikey during transmission.
- Restrict access via firewall if exposing the Web UI beyond localhost.
